# Ripgrep configuration file
# This makes ripgrep behave more like traditional grep by default

# Add type definitions
--type-add=web:*.{html,css,js,jsx,ts,tsx,vue,svelte}
--type-add=config:*.{json,yaml,yml,toml,ini,conf,cfg}

# Set default options
--smart-case
--hidden
--follow
# Do not full-text scan the nix store. Unscoped `rg /nix/store` ran for 30s+
# without finishing and drove the devbox to load 70 (PSI io full=40%); with this
# line it prunes in ~43ms. --follow is KEPT deliberately: home-manager symlinks
# ~/.config/* into the store, and dropping --follow silently hides those configs.
# To search the store on purpose, re-include it: rg --glob='**/nix/store/**' ...
--glob=!**/nix/store/**
--glob=!.git/
--glob=!node_modules/
--glob=!target/
--glob=!dist/
--glob=!build/
--glob=!*.min.js
--glob=!*.map
--max-columns=150
--max-columns-preview

# Use colors
--colors=line:fg:yellow
--colors=line:style:bold
--colors=path:fg:green
--colors=path:style:bold
--colors=match:fg:red
--colors=match:style:bold